{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review enforcement of health & safety rules on prolonged standing in pharmacies",
        "additional_details": "Some workplaces currently impose blanket standing-only policies. Many pharmacies, for example,  open seven days a week. Staff are expected to stand for most of their 8\u201310-hour shifts, even when duties can safely be performed seated. \r\n \r\nIn many workplaces, no suitable chair is available at all. Prolonged standing can contribute to back pain, leg swelling, varicose veins and musculoskeletal problems. We believe staff should not have to develop health problems before being allowed to sit and existing seating rules need stronger enforcement to protect staff without compromising patient safety.",
        "background": "Review the application and enforcement of Regulation 11 of the Workplace (Health, Safety and Welfare) Regulations 1992 to ensure that workplaces provide suitable ergonomic seating with back support and allow pharmacy staff to use it when duties can safely be performed seated.",
